<!--Post: 7307--><!--Time: 1108392444-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7307"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 6:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My opinion only!!! <BR> <BR>BTK demanded this be done. Specific day and time so that he was sure not to miss it. It wouldn&#39;t surprise me if there was a threat if this demand wasn&#39;t met. Not a threat to kill, more along the lines of a threat to cut off communication. Maybe even a promise to reveal more. <BR> <BR>This just sounds like a BTK move to me, not a KAKE move. He wants to push his exposure to the max. I don&#39;t think KAKE or LE would announce something like this. If they had decided to reveal anything it would be done via press conference just like any other time information has been passed on to the public. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve had a theory for a long time involving the Wichita media, but that&#39;s another topic, huh? <BR> <BR>The chess game continues. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7307-->
<!--Post: 7308--><!--Time: 1108394155-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7308"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe this story substantiates my theory a little. Seems the media is trying very hard to please BTK by giving him exposure. <BR> <BR>Their statement &#34;we hope you keep communicating&#34; also tells me that his communications have eluded to the fact that if he is not pleased with the media coverage he will stop communicating with them. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
