<!--Post: 7548--><!--Time: 1108570312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7548"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wannaknow<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wannaknow<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 8:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In KAKE-TV&#39;s recent article on their website &#40;tried unsuccessfully to add a link to it&#41; about the case being on CNN&#39;s Paula Zahn&#39;s show the last sentence reads: &#34;KAKE will continue to communicate with BTK and cover the story through its final chapter.&#34; I find this very interesting that they worded it this way &#40;possibly a message to BTK?&#41;.  No doubt, as has been mentioned, BTK is the mastermind behind this media drama but I also get the feeling &#40;IMO&#41; that because they used the words &#34;final chapter&#34; that there WILL be an end to this sometime soon.  We&#39;ll have to see what this next disclosure reveals tonight. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7548-->
<!--Post: 7550--><!--Time: 1108571113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7550"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 8:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wanna, I saw that too!  It really stuck out at me as well...the word &#34;chapter.&#34; <BR> <BR>Right when you posted this thread on Saturday morning, my first question was WHY are they &#40;KAKE&#41; advertising that many days in advance that they are going to be disclosing this information AND wouldn&#39;t the police need to be involved?  At first, I thought it to be sensational and rate grabbing, but now I think there is a lot more to it.   <BR> <BR>I have a feeling that there are some pretty big FBI honchos working right alongside WPD and KAKE, that there have been more communications, and that we will &#42;&#42;hopefully&#42;&#42; see an end to this soon.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7550-->
<!--Post: 7563--><!--Time: 1108580288-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7563"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 10:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just got a breaking news e-mail from one of the other news outlets in town KWCH Channel 12.  Apparently, another letter or package has been delivered, this time to KSAS-TV Channel 24.  According to the e-mail, mail handlers alerted police and the police took the letter or package for further investigation.   <BR> <BR>It&#39;s interesting that this happened the same day that KAKE is supposed to release the info on 7 and 8. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s the text of the e-mail. <BR> <BR>KWCH 12 Eyewitness News Breaking News <BR>Possible BTK Package <BR> <BR>Wichita police are investigating a possible new communication from BTK-- a mailing to KSAS-TV Wednesday morning. Two employees from Fox Kansas going through the mail discovered it, which contains items that may be from BTK. <BR> <BR>At police request, Eyewitness News is not revealing the contents. Workers called police, who took it as evidence. Investigators are looking over the mailing to determine whether it is from BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7563-->
<!--Post: 7564--><!--Time: 1108580586-->
