<!--/Post: 7567-->
<!--Post: 7568--><!--Time: 1108582084-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7568"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 11:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is a link to a poster Wheathin who seems to get inside info......very curious if you ask me. He or she posted that &#34;one&#34; of the stations got a letter. This poster <b>always</b> seems to have a heads up.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5844.1&amp;search=y" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag =kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5844.1&amp;search=y</a> <BR> <BR>This poster out of all the posters over there kinda creeps me out. Not so much in what they have to say as the style of writing and always seeming to have good inside information. Not a LOT of inside info but enough to know for sure that his person is on the inside in some way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
