<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7606"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kwch 12 just had the btk story. The package was sent to KWCH&#39;s sister station KSAS Fox 24. The news is broadcast from Channel 12&#39;s station in north Wichita..&#40;37th st. north&#41; The package was found in the mail at the Fox business location on North West street. It had several stamps and that is what caught the attention of the two workers who found it. The postcard said something to the effect of he&#40;btk&#41; think KAKE is a good station nd all but that they were being singled out because of all of the attention lately...etc. The package looked like a brown postal envelope type, smaller in size than the last one. I think thay said something about a picture and some jewelry and a picture being inside. No video link up yet. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
