<!--Post: 7661--><!--Time: 1108649250-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7661"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Vscantu - those were my words. Not everything was released about the postcards. <BR> <BR>Local media feel that C.4 and C.9 refer to the chapters just as Hbtcontrol stated. <BR> <BR>KAKE news made the comment that the cereal boxes were found close to where Davis was killed. They stated that Davis was also missing jewelry. They didn&#39;t say the jewelry was Davis&#39;. That is just the assumption that is being made locally. There is supposed to be a new statement made by LE at 10:00 this morning. <BR> <BR>If boxes #7, #8 and package #11 contained jewelry and none of it was Nancy Fox&#39;s, then how many murders is he claiming? How many crimes in this area are missing jewelry?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7661-->
<!--Post: 7662--><!--Time: 1108649311-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7662"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not being a Wichitan, I missed what KAKE reported last night as to the contents of drops #7 &amp; #8.  Could someone please summarize the story?  Thank you.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7662-->
<!--Post: 7665--><!--Time: 1108650000-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7665"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The main thing that was released was info that was on the postcard that was sent to KAKE alerting them to communications #7 and #8. They released the following information <BR> <BR>Contents: C.9, Jewelry <BR> <BR>KAKE said there were other contents as well but they were asked not to release them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
