<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7723"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Amandab<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Amandab<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wilmac- <BR> <BR>Perhaps his next 2 communications will contain the next 3 and 4 digits, respectively? I&#39;m not sure how the phone systems work, but couldn&#39;t the next 3 digits of the phone number narrow the field significantly? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
